        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nMICHAEL G. FRICK, ESQ., Brunswick, Georgia; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nDAN HIMMELFARB, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is recharacterization pretty much of a judge-made thing? There's -- there's no statute that provides for it, is there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Michael G. Frick)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, it is our contention that, as in the Adams and Miller cases from the Second and Third Circuits, that at the present time, under the restrictions of the AEDPA, that a recharacterization should never take place by a court unless there is concurrence on the part of the petitioner himself and he's given the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frick",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Rehnquist, there are circumstances I understand, not from personal knowledge, where recharacterization does take place in spite of the fact that there is an attorney. But the actual process and -- and the recharacterizations that have taken place over the years have been for the benefit of a pro se prisoner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unknown Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is recharacterization done only with pro se litigants? If I were an attorney, I'm not sure I'd be terribly happy to have a lawyer -- to have the judge say, well, this is the wrong kind of writ, I'm going to treat it thus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals denied authorization to file the motion under 2244(b)(3)(E). This Court lacks jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: In principle, you have no objection. What about in practice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have no objection insofar as there's a requirement that he be notified of how it would be treated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't think there should be warnings about the consequences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To the extent that the Court wishes to impose a notice requirement, our view is that it should go essentially like this. It is important to recharacterize a post-conviction motion not styled a 2255 motion if it seeks relief available only under 2255."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:56 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
      "case_id": "2003-02-6683",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It also serves the interest of vindicating Congress' purpose in enacting the bar on second or successive motions in AEDPA."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
